          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Lorck's love for Constance as a true and serious emotional state. The continuation emphasizes that he has newly recognized its depth.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal introduces and grounds an integrated offer of Lorck's whole self, life, and soul, for which he asks Constance's acceptance. Thus it participates in affirming a proposed relational bond rather than merely sitting near an unrelated promise. The undertaking is substantial but figurative and lacks specific practical terms.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"nNej, uf nej,* sa hun, og veg uvilkaarlig\\ntilbage.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.78,\"reason\":\"The declaration occurs amid an agitated, insistent confrontation and has some force as an affective outpouring. Nevertheless, its deliberate assertion of seriousness and its articulated offer make avowal and undertaking—not reflex-like discharge—the dominant modes.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Han stødte Foden haardt i Gulvet, idet han\\ntraadte et Skridt nærmere.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"No distinct residual core force is needed: the occurrence is adequately characterized as a serious avowal embedded in an offer of relational self-commitment, with limited expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Lorck declares his love directly to Constance during an unwanted and increasingly coercive advance. After she has resisted and asked him to stop, he insists that his love is serious, offers her himself, his life, and his soul, and asks whether she will accept. Constance immediately refuses and withdraws.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Lorck's declaration is integrated with a figurative but serious offer of himself, his life, and his soul, positioning him as committed to a proposed intimate bond. Its concrete obligations remain unspecified. Constance explicitly rejects the offer—“Nej, uf nej”—and moves back, so there is no mutual undertaking or acceptance.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the work from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents Lorck as intensely infatuated, but it does not independently settle the durability or benevolence of his feelings. His coercive conduct complicates the character of the affection without removing the avowing or offer-making force of the focal occurrence.\"}"
        }
